## Key Features

1. **Offline Data Storage**: Uses AsyncStorage to save surveys locally when offline
2. **Pending Sync Queue**: Maintains a queue of surveys that need to be synced
3. **Automatic Sync**: Attempts to sync when connection is restored or periodically
4. **Network Awareness**: Shows offline status and sync status to users
5. **Conflict Resolution**: Marks surveys as synced after successful upload
6. **Periodic Sync**: Regularly checks for pending surveys to sync

## Additional Considerations

1. **Error Handling**: Comprehensive error handling for both offline and online operations
2. **Performance**: Efficient data management to handle large numbers of surveys
3. **Security**: Consider adding encryption for sensitive survey data
4. **Data Validation**: Add validation before saving or syncing data
5. **Background Sync**: For more robust syncing, consider using background tasks

This implementation provides a solid foundation for an offline-first field surveying app with automatic sync capabilities. You can extend it with additional features like GPS location tracking, photo attachments, and more complex survey forms as needed.

# Offline-First Field Surveying App with Sync Capabilities

Below is a comprehensive implementation of an offline-first field surveying app that syncs data when reconnected to the internet. This example uses React Native for the mobile interface, but the core concepts can be adapted to other platforms.

## Core Architecture

```javascript
// App.js - Main Application Component
import React, { useState, useEffect } from 'react';
import { View, Text, StyleSheet, Button, Alert } from 'react-native';
import AsyncStorage from '@react-native-async-storage/async-storage';
import NetInfo from '@react-native-community/netinfo';
import SurveyForm from './components/SurveyForm';
import SyncManager from './services/SyncManager';

const App = () => {
  const [isConnected, setIsConnected] = useState(false);
  const [pendingSyncCount, setPendingSyncCount] = useState(0);
  const [surveys, setSurveys] = useState([]);

  // Initialize sync manager
  const syncManager = new SyncManager();

  useEffect(() => {
    // Load local surveys
    loadLocalSurveys();

    // Set up network listener
    const unsubscribe = NetInfo.addEventListener(state => {
      setIsConnected(state.isConnected);
      if (state.isConnected) {
        syncPendingData();
      }
    });

    return () => unsubscribe();
  }, []);

  const loadLocalSurveys = async () => {
    try {
      const storedSurveys = await AsyncStorage.getItem('localSurveys');
      if (storedSurveys) {
        setSurveys(JSON.parse(storedSurveys));
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error loading local surveys:', error);
    }
  };

  const saveSurveyLocally = async (surveyData) => {
    try {
      const newSurveys = [...surveys, surveyData];
      await AsyncStorage.setItem('localSurveys', JSON.stringify(newSurveys));
      setSurveys(newSurveys);
      Alert.alert('Success', 'Survey saved locally');
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Error saving survey:', error);
      Alert.alert('Error', 'Failed to save survey locally');
    }
  };

  const syncPendingData = async () => {
    try {
      const pendingCount = await syncManager.syncAllPending();
      setPendingSyncCount(pendingCount);
      if (pendingCount > 0) {
        Alert.alert('Sync Complete', `${pendingCount} surveys synced successfully`);
        await loadLocalSurveys(); // Refresh local data after sync
      }
    } catch (error) {
      console.error('Sync error:', error);
      Alert.alert('Sync Error', 'Failed to sync data');
    }
  };

  const handleSurveySubmit = async (surveyData) => {
    if (isConnected) {
      // Directly sync if online
      try {
        await syncManager.syncSurvey(surveyData);
        Alert.alert('Success', 'Survey submitted successfully');
      } catch (error) {
        console.error('Sync error:', error);
        Alert.alert('Error', 'Failed to submit survey');
      }
    } else {
      // Save locally if offline
      await saveSurveyLocally(surveyData);
      setPendingSyncCount(pendingSyncCount + 1);
    }
  };

  return (
    <View style={styles.container}>
      <Text style={styles.title}>Field Survey App</Text>
      <View style={styles.statusContainer}>
        <Text style={styles.statusText}>
          Status: {isConnected ? 'Online' : 'Offline'}
        </Text>
        {pendingSyncCount > 0 && (
          <Text style={styles.pendingText}>
            {pendingSyncCount} surveys pending sync
          </Text>
        )}
      </View>

      <SurveyForm onSubmit={handleSurveySubmit} />

      {!isConnected && (
        <View style={styles.offlineNotice}>
          <Text style={styles.offlineText}>
            You're offline. Surveys will be saved locally and synced when you reconnect.
          </Text>
        </View>
      )}
    </View>
  );
};

const styles = StyleSheet.create({
  container: {
    flex: 1,
    padding: 20,
    backgroundColor: '#f5f5f5',
  },
  title: {
    fontSize: 24,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
    marginBottom: 20,
    textAlign: 'center',
  },
  statusContainer: {
    marginBottom: 20,
    padding: 10,
    backgroundColor: '#e0e0e0',
    borderRadius: 5,
  },
  statusText: {
    fontSize: 16,
    fontWeight: 'bold',
  },
  pendingText: {
    fontSize: 14,
    color: '#d32f2f',
    marginTop: 5,
  },
