# Minimal Real-Time 3D Scene Viewer with Dynamic Lighting and Shaders

Here's a minimal working version of a 3D scene viewer using WebGL (via Three.js) that includes dynamic lighting and shader effects. This example creates a simple scene with a rotating cube and a point light that moves with the mouse.

## HTML File (index.html)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>Minimal 3D Scene Viewer</title>
    <style>
        body { margin: 0; overflow: hidden; }
        canvas { display: block; }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/three@0.132.2/build/three.min.js"></script>
    <script src="app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

## JavaScript File (app.js)

```javascript
// Scene setup
const scene = new THREE.Scene();
const camera = new THREE.PerspectiveCamera(75, window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight, 0.1, 1000);
const renderer = new THREE.WebGLRenderer({ antialias: true });
renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
document.body.appendChild(renderer.domElement);

// Create a cube with a custom shader material
const geometry = new THREE.BoxGeometry(2, 2, 2);

// Custom shader material for the cube
const cubeMaterial = new THREE.ShaderMaterial({
    uniforms: {
        time: { value: 0 },
        lightPosition: { value: new THREE.Vector3(0, 0, 0) }
    },
    vertexShader: `
        uniform float time;
        varying vec3 vNormal;
        varying vec3 vPosition;

        void main() {
            vNormal = normalize(normalMatrix * normal);
            vPosition = position;

            // Simple vertex animation
            float wave = sin(position.y * 2.0 + time * 2.0) * 0.2;
            vec3 newPosition = position + normal * wave;

            gl_Position = projectionMatrix * modelViewMatrix * vec4(newPosition, 1.0);
        }
    `,
    fragmentShader: `
        uniform float time;
        uniform vec3 lightPosition;
        varying vec3 vNormal;
        varying vec3 vPosition;

        void main() {
            // Calculate lighting
            vec3 lightDir = normalize(lightPosition - vPosition);
            float diffuse = max(dot(vNormal, lightDir), 0.0);

            // Base color with lighting
            vec3 color = vec3(0.2, 0.5, 0.8) * (0.5 + diffuse * 0.5);

            // Add some color variation based on position
            color += sin(vPosition.x * 5.0 + time) * 0.1;
            color += sin(vPosition.y * 5.0 + time * 0.7) * 0.1;
            color += sin(vPosition.z * 5.0 + time * 1.3) * 0.1;

            gl_FragColor = vec4(color, 1.0);
        }
    `,
    side: THREE.DoubleSide
});

const cube = new THREE.Mesh(geometry, cubeMaterial);
scene.add(cube);

// Create a point light (not visible, but affects the shader)
const pointLight = new THREE.PointLight(0xffffff, 1, 100);
scene.add(pointLight);

// Camera position
camera.position.z = 5;

// Animation variables
let time = 0;
const mouse = { x: 0, y: 0 };

// Handle window resize
window.addEventListener('resize', () => {
    camera.aspect = window.innerWidth / window.innerHeight;
    camera.updateProjectionMatrix();
    renderer.setSize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
});

// Handle mouse movement
window.addEventListener('mousemove', (event) => {
    mouse.x = (event.clientX / window.innerWidth) * 2 - 1;
    mouse.y = -(event.clientY / window.innerHeight) * 2 + 1;
});

// Animation loop
function animate() {
    requestAnimationFrame(animate);

    // Update time
    time += 0.01;
    cubeMaterial.uniforms.time.value = time;

    // Rotate the cube
    cube.rotation.x += 0.005;
    cube.rotation.y += 0.005;

    // Move light with mouse
    pointLight.position.set(mouse.x * 5, mouse.y * 5, 3);
    cubeMaterial.uniforms.lightPosition.value.copy(pointLight.position);

    renderer.render(scene, camera);
}

animate();
```

## Features

1. **Basic 3D Scene**: A rotating cube with a custom shader material
2. **Dynamic Lighting**: A point light that follows the mouse position
3. **Shader Effects**:
   - Vertex animation (wave effect)
   - Custom lighting calculation in the fragment shader
   - Color variation based on position and time
4. **Responsive Design**: Adjusts to window size changes

